Third-party notices
====================

This file names components the desktop package ships or links that are not
covered by the Apache License 2.0 grant in LICENSE. It is not a complete scan
of every transitive dependency.

whisper.cpp
-----------

The desktop app stages a whisper.cpp transcription binary (MIT License).
The binary is built from an upstream pin; the whisper.cpp LICENSE text is not
vendored next to the binary. Copyright remains with the whisper.cpp authors.
See https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp

sharp / libvips
---------------

The desktop image pipeline uses the npm package `sharp`, which links libvips.
libvips is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 3 or later (LGPL-3.0-or-later). That license is not Apache 2.0.
A recipient who wants the corresponding library source can use the version
recorded in the desktop lockfile.

